{
  "name": "CAD check - remove finished yes rows (dry run by default)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c352b09d-5656-472a-8d4e-fdc29a145503",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3248,
        1136
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "height": 330,
        "width": 760,
        "content": "## Remove finished rows from the CAD check tab (answer yes or no)\n\nLeaves only the rows that still need attention (the 'no' rows). dryRun true (default) only reports how many rows would go and which stay.\n\ndryRun false: first copies every row it is about to delete to a tab 'CAD check done (yes)' (all columns, with the date), then deletes those rows from the CAD check tab. If the copy fails, nothing is deleted. Rows with a blank or other answer in column F are never touched.\n\nConfig: answer (yes = default, or no), keepFiles (comma list of drawing files whose rows stay, e.g. rows still needing a decision), reviewTab (CAD check), tabs (blank = all, or e.g. Bathtub,Marble+ Basin: only yes rows of these tabs). Run it after the CAD pictures of those products are live on Shopify."
      }
    },
